<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - April 18.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - April 18.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 04/18/97  04/11/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East		8.82	8.81     3.79	 3.79	4.1</p>
<p>West	     47.87     45.25    18.47	17.46     31.4</p>
<p>Total Canada   56.69     54.06    11.53	11.00     19.0</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 04/18/97: 232.55 bcf, 04/11/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 04/18/97: 259.11 bcf, 04/11/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
